Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:48:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 249/260] [ae-patch] Recognise the forwarder's own posts when
 the tunnel names no item id

A single transcript item goes over the runner's event tunnel, whose acknowledgement carries no item id, so the forwarder never learned the ids of its own posts and every row after the seed looked foreign; the transcript keep's record never advanced and every relaunch rebuilt. The forwarder now derives the id from the post's source id with the server's own formula when the post returns none, a real returned id still wins, and a source id that is empty or over 256 characters is never derived. It records the kind of each item it posts (type, plus role for a message) and counts an id as its own only for a server row of that kind, so a row that reuses the id under another type or role still holds the record. The record logs once per foreign item why it is held, and warns once per session about a post it cannot recognise.
